 story is not unique; I have heard similar tales countless times. The pins =
and needles, the numbness, the deep, aching pain that flares up when darkne=
ss falls. Too often, these patients are dismissed with the advice to simply=
 endure their suffering.</p>
                                    <p style=3D"margin: 0 0 18px 0;">I refu=
se to accept that. Over the years, I have developed a straightforward appro=
ach that has empowered many of my patients to reclaim their nights and alle=
viate their discomfort. This method is uncomplicated and can be practiced r=
ight at home.</p>
                                    <p style=3D"margin: 0 0 18px 0;">When I=
 shared this approach with Ruth, her transformation was remarkable. A few w=
eeks later, she returned, radiating a newfound vitality. She was sleeping s=
oundly through the night and had resumed her morning walks with her dog. Wi=
th gratitude in her eyes, she reached across my desk, took my hand, and tha=
nked me.</p>
